# Ray's runtime_env working_dir auto-upload ignore file (same syntax as
# .gitignore). Without this, `ray.init()` (called implicitly by any
# RayRLlib-based solver/test) tries to zip and upload the entire repo
# working directory to the local Ray cluster on every run -- 2.3GB+ here,
# mostly test/build data ray never needs for single-machine local runs:
#   - cpp/tests/data/pddl/  (git submodule, real IPC benchmark PDDL files, ~2.2GB)
#   - .venv/                (~2.6GB)
#   - .git/                 (~490MB)
#   - cpp/sdk/              (vendored C++ dependencies, build artifacts)
# Exceeding ray's default 512MB runtime_env package size warning/limit is
# what this file prevents.
.venv/
.git/
cpp/sdk/
cpp/tests/data/
build/
dist/
node_modules/
*.pddl
